Expense Tracker App

A full-stack mobile expense tracker that lets users sign up, sign in, and log their income and expenses in real time. The app automatically calculates the user's current balance, total income, and total expenses based on their transaction history.

Live Backend

The backend API is deployed on Render:
https://expense-tracker-app-server-qu4y.onrender.com

Features
Secure authentication with email/password sign-up and sign-in, including email verification and two-factor authentication (powered by Clerk)
Add new transactions as either income or expense, with category tagging
Automatic real-time calculation of balance, total income, and total expenses
View and delete recent transactions
Persistent cloud storage using PostgreSQL
Rate-limited backend API to prevent abuse
Tech Stack

Frontend (Mobile App)

React Native
Expo / Expo Router
Clerk (authentication)

Backend (Server)

Node.js
Express
PostgreSQL via Neon (serverless)
Upstash Redis (rate limiting)
Project Structure
Expense_Tracker_App/
├── mobile/     # React Native / Expo frontend
└── backend/    # Node.js / Express backend
Prerequisites

Before setting up locally, make sure you have installed:

Node.js (v20 or later recommended)
npm (comes with Node.js)
Expo Go app on your phone (for quick testing) or Android Studio / Xcode (for emulators)
A Clerk account (for authentication keys)
A Neon account (for the PostgreSQL database)
An Upstash account (for Redis rate limiting)
Backend Setup
Navigate to the backend folder:
   cd backend
Install dependencies:
   npm install
Create a .env file in the backend folder with the following variables:
   PORT=5001
   DATABASE_URL=your_neon_postgresql_connection_string
   UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=your_upstash_redis_url
   UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=your_upstash_redis_token
   API_URL=http://localhost:5001
Start the server:
   npm run dev

The server will run on http://localhost:5001 by default.

Mobile App Setup
Navigate to the mobile folder:
   cd mobile
Install dependencies:
   npm install
Create a .env file in the mobile folder with the following variables:
   EXPO_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your_clerk_publishable_key
   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:5001

Get your Clerk publishable key from the Clerk Dashboard under API Keys.

Start the Expo development server:
   npx expo start
Scan the QR code with the Expo Go app on your phone, or press a to open on an Android emulator.
Building a Standalone APK

This project uses EAS Build to create installable APK files that run without a development server.

Install the EAS CLI:
   npm install -g eas-cli
Log in to your Expo account:
   eas login
Make sure your eas.json includes your environment variables under the relevant build profile (since .env files are not uploaded to EAS build servers):
jsonc
   "preview": {
     "distribution": "internal",
     "env": {
       "EXPO_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY": "your_clerk_publishable_key",
       "EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL": "https://expense-tracker-app-server-qu4y.onrender.com"
     }
   }
Run the build:
   eas build --profile preview --platform android
Once the build finishes, download and install the .apk file on your Android device.
Notes
For a standalone (non-development) build, EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL should point to the deployed backend (Render URL above), not localhost, since the app will no longer have access to your local machine.
Development builds require a running Metro server (npx expo start --dev-client) and a device connection (WiFi or USB via adb reverse).